nscripts and Testimony L570: # Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure\nL571: \nL572: The Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure govern procedure in the United States courts of appeals.\nL573: \nL574: The Supreme Court first adopted the Rules of Appellate Procedure by order dated December 4, 1967, transmitted to Congress on January 15, 1968, and effective July 1, 1968. The Appellate Rules and accompanying forms were last amended in 2025.\nL575: \nL576:   * Read the cite198†Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure (PDF)\nL577: ## Official Forms\nL578: \nL579: The appellate rules forms are officially published in an Appendix of Forms accompanying the Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure.\nL580: Word-Processing Templates: For user convenience, the Administrative Office Forms Working Group of judges and clerks has recommended making available to the public the unofficial Word versions linked below. Given their nature, language in these forms may require modification before the document can be filed with the court. These forms are therefore offered as templates based on the official published forms.\nL581:   * Appellate Form 1A. Notice of Appeal to a Court of Appeals From a Judgment of a District Court. (cite199†word )\nL582:   * Appellate Form 1B. Notice of Appeal to a Court of Appeals From an Appealable Order of a District Court. (cite200†word )\nL583:   * Appellate Form 2. Notice of Appeal to a Court of Appeals From a Decision of the United States Tax Court. (cite201†word )\nL584:   * Appellate Form 3. Petition for Review of Order of an Agency, Board, Commission or Officer. (cite202†word )\nL585:   * Appellate Form 4. Affidavit Accompanying Motion for Permission to Appeal In Forma Pauperis. (cite203†word )\nL586:   * Appellate Form 5. Notice of Appeal to a Court of Appeals from a Judgment or Order of a District Court or a Bankruptcy Appellate Panel. (cite204†word )\nL587:   * Appellate Form 6. Certificate of Compliance With Type-Volume Limit. (cite205†word )\nL588:   * Appellate Form 7. Declaration of Inmate Filing. (cite206†word )\nL589:   * Appendix: Length Limits Stated in the Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure. (cite207†word )\nL590: cite185†Return to top L591: \nL592:   * cite208†Glossary of Legal Terms L593:   * cite209†Careers L594:   * cite210†FAQs L595:   * cite211†Contact Us L596: \nL597: cite212†Image L598: \nL599: This site is maintained by the Administrative Office of the U.S. Courts on behalf of the Federal Judiciary.\nL600: \nL601:   * cite213†Privacy & Security Policy L602:   * cite214†Operating Status L603:   * cite215†Download Plug-Ins L604: \nL605: To receive updates, enter your email address and select the topics that interest you.\nL606: \nL607: Your browser does not support Javascript. Your browser does not support Javascript.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFederal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure (https://www.uscourts.gov/forms-rules/current-rules-practice-procedure/federal-rules-bankruptcy-procedure)\nciteturn951view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn943view8\",\"pattern\":\"pdf\"}); Total lines: 626\nL551:     * cite165†Committee Reports L552:     * cite166†Congressional and Supreme Court Rules Packages L553:     * cite167†FJC Studies and Related Publications L554:     * cite168†Meeting Minutes L555:     * cite169†Past Members of the Rules Committees L556:     * cite170†Preliminary Drafts of Proposed Rule Amendments L557:     * cite171†Rules Comments L558:       * cite191†Archive of Proposed Rule and Form Amendments on Regulations.gov L559:     * cite172†Rules Suggestions L560:     * cite173†Special Projects of the Rules Committees L561:       * cite192†2010 Civil Litigation Conference L562:       * cite193†Civil Rule 23 Mini-Conference L563:       * cite194†Dallas Conference on Preservation/Sanctions (9/9/11) L564:       * cite195†Invitation for Comment on Emergency Rulemaking L565:       * cite196†Invitation for Comment on Privilege Log Practice L566:       * cite197†Mini-Conference on Waiver of Attorney-Client Privilege and Work-Product Doctrine L567:     * cite174†Style Resources L568:     * cite175†Superseded Rules Pamphlets L569:     * cite176†Transcripts and Testimony L570: # Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure\nL571: \nL572: The Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure govern procedures for bankruptcy proceedings.\nL573: For many years, such proceedings were governed by the General Orders and Forms in Bankruptcy promulgated by the Supreme Court. By order dated April 24, 1973, effective October 1, 1973, the Supreme Court prescribed, pursuant to 28 U.S.C. § 2075, the Bankruptcy Rules and Official Bankruptcy Forms, which abrogated previous rules and forms. The Bankruptcy Rules and Official Forms were last amended in 2025.\nL574: \nL575:   * Read the cite198†Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure (PDF)\nL576: ## Interim Bankruptcy Rule 1007-I\nL577: The National Guard and Reservists Debt Relief Act of 2008, Pub. L. No. 110-438, as amended by Public Law No. 118-24, provides a temporary exclusion from the bankruptcy means test for certain reservists and members of the National Guard.\nL578: At the request of the Judicial Conference's Advisory Committee on Bankruptcy Rules, cite199†Interim Rule 1007-I (PDF) was transmitted to the courts for adoption as a local rule to implement the temporary exclusion. The temporary exclusion originally went into effect for three years on December 19, 2008. It has been extended several times by Congress, most recently until December 19, 2027.\nL579: ## Interim Bankruptcy Rule 1020\nL580: \nL581: (Inapplicable to cases filed after June 21, 2024)\nL582: On June 21, 2022, the Bankruptcy Threshold and Technical Corrections Act (BTATC Act), Pub. L.\nL583: 117-151 temporarily set, until June 21, 2024, the total debt limit for determining eligibility of a debtor to proceed under subchapter V of chapter 11 to $7,500,000 – the amount previously in effect for several years under the CARES Act. cite200†Interim Bankruptcy Rule 1020 (PDF) was drafted to implement that temporary $7,500,000 BTATC Act debt limit, and courts were encouraged to adopt the Interim Rule as a local rule while the BTATC debt limits were in effect.\nL584: Because the BTATCA debt limit for subchapter V cases expired on June 21, 2024, Interim Rule 1020 is not applicable to cases filed after that date. With respect to cases filed after June 21, 2024, the applicable debt limit for subchapter V cases is the same as that for a small business case as defined in 11 U.S.C. § 101(51D) - $3,024,725 (amount subject to adjustment on 4/01/25 and every three years after that).\nL585: ## Bankruptcy Rules (rules 1001 to 9037)\nL586: \nL587: Refer to the United States Code, Title 11, Bankruptcy.\nL588: \nL589: cite201†Rule 1001. Scope of Rules and Forms; Short Title†uscode.house.gov L590: \nL591: cite202†Part I—Commencement of Case; Proceedings Relating To Petition And Order For Relief (rules 1002 to 1021)†uscode.house.gov L592: \nL593: cite203†Part II—Officers And Administration; Notices; Meetings; Examinations; Elections; Attorneys And Accountants (rules 2001 to 2020)†uscode.house.gov L594: cite204†Part III—Claims And Distribution To Creditors And Equity Interest Holders; Plans (rules 3001 to 3022)†uscode.house.gov L595: \nL596: cite205†Part IV—The Debtor: Duties And Benefits (rules 4001 to 4008)†uscode.house.gov L597: \nL598: cite206†Part V—Courts And Clerks (rules 5001 to 5012)†uscode.house.gov L599: \nL600: cite207†Part VI—Collection And Liquidation Of The Estate (rules 6001 to 6011)†uscode.house.gov L601: \nL602: cite208†Part VII—Adversary Proceedings (rule 7001 to 7087†uscode.house.gov L603: cite209†Part VIII—Appeals To District Court Or Bankruptcy Appellate Panel (rules 8001 to 8028)†uscode.house.gov L604: \nL605: cite210†Part IX—General Provisions (rules 9001 to 9037)†uscode.house.gov L606: \nL607: Part X—United States Trustees [Abrogated (Apr. 30, 1991, eff. Aug. 1, 1991).]\nL608: \nL609: cite185†Return to top L610: \nL611:   * cite211†Glossary of Legal Terms L612:   * cite212†Careers L613:   * cite213†FAQs L614:   * cite214†Contact Us L615: \nL616: cite215†Image L617: \nL618: This site is maintained by the Administrative Office of the U.S. Courts on behalf of the Federal Judiciary.\nL619:   * cite216†Privacy & Security Policy L620:   * cite217†Operating Status L621:   * cite218†Download Plug-Ins L622: \nL623: To receive updates, enter your email address and select the topics that interest you.\nL624: \nL625: Your browser does not support Javascript. Your browser does not support Javascript.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCongressional Rules Package - 2026 (https://www.uscourts.gov/forms-rules/records-rules-committees/packages-submitted/congressional-rules-package-2026)\nciteturn951view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn882view3\",\"pattern\":\"Attachments\"}); Total lines: 604\nNo matching text found for \"Attachments\""
